---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Trade90V2Layout.astro";
import Finder from "../../components/Trade90PairFinder.svelte";
import {allTrade90Pairs,majors,crosses,pairUrl,rateSnapshot,reportDate} from "../../lib/trade90-v3.js";
---
<Layout title="Forex Pair Research: 28 Currency Comparisons" description="Explore 28 dedicated forex currency pair research pages. See policy-rate divergence, two-bank source records, forward pricing status and upcoming decisions." canonical="/pairs/">
<main class="wrap">
<header class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">28 pair research hubs</div><h1>Explore a Forex Currency Pair</h1><p>Choose a pair to compare its two central banks, current official interest-rate difference, next decisions and verified publications. Policy rates checked {reportDate(rateSnapshot.asOf)}.</p></header>
<Finder client:load pairs={allTrade90Pairs} limit={28}/>
<section><div class="head"><h2>USD major pairs</h2><a href="/rate-gaps/">Full rate comparison →</a></div><div class="grid">{majors.map(p=><a href={pairUrl(p.symbol)}><strong>{p.label}</strong><small>{p.baseBank.short} / {p.quoteBank.short}</small><span>Research →</span></a>)}</div></section>
<section><div class="head"><h2>Cross-currency pairs</h2></div><div class="grid">{crosses.map(p=><a href={pairUrl(p.symbol)}><strong>{p.label}</strong><small>{p.baseBank.short} / {p.quoteBank.short}</small><span>Research →</span></a>)}</div></section>
<p class="caveat">Research is informational, not a trading signal. All 28 pair links lead to their own source-dated rate comparison.</p>
<section class="article"><h2>How to use these currency-pair pages</h2><p>Start with the two currencies in the pair. The first is the base currency and the second is the quote currency. Each research page compares their selected central-bank benchmarks, shows the signed rate gap and links to the underlying policy sources. A positive gap means the base benchmark is higher; it does not mean the base currency will rise.</p><p>The economic comparison charts add inflation, unemployment and real GDP context. Check each observation date and reporting frequency before comparing values. A monthly inflation release and a quarterly growth release describe different periods, and historical observations can be revised.</p><p>Use the <a href="/decisions/">decision calendar</a> to identify the next scheduled announcements and the <a href="/central-banks/">central-bank pages</a> to read the relevant publications. Our <a href="/learn/what-is-interest-rate-divergence/">interest-rate divergence guide</a> explains the basic calculation and its limitations.</p></section>
</main>
</Layout>
<style>.head{margin-top:35px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px}.head h2{font-size:1.35rem}.head a{font-size:.8rem}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:11px;margin:8px 0 25px}.grid a{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;border:1px solid #334155;border-radius:11px;background:#111c30;padding:17px;text-decoration:none;color:#f8fafc}.grid a:hover{border-color:#3b82f6;background:#192c38}.grid strong{font-size:1.12rem}.grid small{color:#94a3b8}.grid span{color:#93c5fd;font-size:.76rem;font-weight:760;margin-top:9px}.caveat{font-size:.78rem;color:#94a3b8}@media(max-width:780px){.grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}}@media(max-width:520px){.grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.grid a{padding:12px}}</style>